1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nicolai Mejdell From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Christian Henrik Nicolai Mejdell (1822 – 1899) was a Norwegian mining engineer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Vang, Hedmark. He took his mining examination in 1843. He worked as manager of Selbu Copper Works and Kongsberg Silver Works, and from 1865 he was the mine superindendent (Norwegian: bergmester) for all of South-Eas
2 CONC tern Norway. He was also an editor-in-chief of the newspaper Christiania-Posten, and issued books.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a nephew of officer Jacob Gerhard Meydell, brother of forester Thorvald Mejdell and the father of jurist and writer Glør Thorvald Mejdell. Through his sister Cecilie Marie Mejdell he was a brother-in-law of Matthias Wilhelm
2 CONC  Sinding and an uncle of Christian, Otto and Stephan Sinding; and also an uncle of Thora Cathrine Sinding who married his son Glør.
