1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tönis grew up in List/Sylt at the house of his aunt, Anna Silvia Leganger who was married to Rasmus Rasmussen Abildgaard, customs control officer, stationed there from 1758 to 1771.
2 CONT His mother Signe had left for Viborg, but had come back to Sylt by 1767 where she gave birth to a second extra-marital child, Gondel. Signe died on Sylt in 1800.
2 CONT Tönis received his helmsmen's license in 1779 in Copenhagen. He became captain very swiftly and built his own house in Tinnum/Sylt in 1784. It still exists and is owned by one of his descendants. He mainly sailed to the West Indie
2 CONC s and to the Mediterranean Sea, under Danish flag.
2 CONT He had seven children with his wife Merreth, three boys and four girls. All three boys became sailors as his father, and went missing at separate occasions, all at early ages. Erich Tönissen died in 1806, Siewert Andreas in autumn
2 CONC  1816 and Andreas Tönis in 1821. Siewert and Andreas however had married early and left children behind.
2 CONT Three of the four daughters reached adulthood and left numerous descendants on the island.
